{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `r`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: vectorized the beta prior for `p` and the binomial likelihood for `r` so that the protected observation is scored exactly once with a plain top-level sampling statement outside loops. Changed `p` from a bounded matrix to an equivalently indexed bounded two-dimensional array of reals to allow direct vectorized sampling as a top-level parameter. Added `mu ~ uniform(0, 1)`, which is density-neutral for a parameter already constrained to `[0, 1]` and satisfies SafeStan's unique-prior requirement. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> G;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[G, N] int<lower=0> r;
  array[G, N] int<lower=0> n;
}
parameters {
  array[G, N] real<lower=0, upper=1> p;
  vector<lower=0, upper=1>[G] mu;
  vector<lower=0.1>[G] a_plus_b;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[G] a;
  vector[G] b;
  array[G, N] real<lower=0> a_rep;
  array[G, N] real<lower=0> b_rep;
  a = mu .* a_plus_b;
  b = (1 - mu) .* a_plus_b;
  for (g in 1 : G) {
    for (i in 1 : N) {
      a_rep[g, i] = a[g];
      b_rep[g, i] = b[g];
    }
  }
}
model {
  mu ~ uniform(0, 1);
  a_plus_b ~ pareto(0.1, 1.5);
  p ~ beta(a_rep, b_rep);
  r ~ binomial(n, p);
}
generated quantities {
  vector<lower=0>[G] theta;
  for (g in 1 : G) {
    theta[g] = 1 / (a[g] + b[g]);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"G":2,"N":2,"n":[[2,2],[4,4]],"r":[[1,0],[0,1]]}","protected_variables":["r"]}
